SUMMARY:Park to Port Bike Ride
DTSTAMP:20260805T111509Z
DTSTART:20261024T080000Z
DESCRIPTION:Hermann Park Conservancy’s 12th annual Park to Port Bike Ride i
	s set for Saturday\, October 24. \nThe 20-mile round-trip bike ride takes 
	cyclists from Hermann Park’s Bayou Parkland along the Bayou Greenway trail
	 all the way to Mason Park\, near the Port of Houston. Enjoy the turn-arou
	nd party\, but be sure to save some energy for a well-deserved post-ride p
	arty under the Bill Coats Bridge! \nPark to Port is open to riders of all 
	skill levels and is not a race. Whether you are an experienced cyclist or 
	are riding just for fun\, you can go at your own pace on this scenic city 
	journey. \nYour participation in Park to Port supports Hermann Park Conser
	vancy and its stewardship efforts for one of Houston’s most beloved parks 
	while promoting the ever-growing Bayou Greenway trail system. \nRegister a
	nd learn more at the following link: 12th Annual Park to Port Bike Ride. E
	arly bird pricing is available until August 17. \nSPECIAL OFFER: Save $10 
	on registration when you sign up for BOTH the Park to Port Bike Ride and R
	un in the Park! Bundle deal is available via the link above. Information o
	n Run in the Park can be found here.\n\nhttps://hermannpark.org/event/park
	-to-port-bike-ride-2/\n\nFrom Hermann Park Conservancy
URL:https://hermannpark.org/event/park-to-port-bike-ride-2/
LOCATION:Bayou Parkland\, 6532 Almeda Rd\, Houston\, TX\, 77021\, United St
	ates
